    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0577" n="567" xml:id="pg567"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 904.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 7, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 23d of March, No. 628,
                    has been received, and your proceedings therein related in regard to the
                    supposed outfit of the screw steamer Amphion are approved. The frank
                    explanations which Earl Russell so properly made upon that subject are
                    appreciated by this government. I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. F. Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
